WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.405 --> 00:00:09.409
[dramatic music playing]

00:00:11.143 --> 00:00:12.645
[Michael]
<i> This is McGill University</i>

00:00:12.678 --> 00:00:14.447
<i> in Montreal, Canada.</i>

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:17.383
It boasts an enrollment of more
than 40,000 students

00:00:17.416 --> 00:00:19.185
from 150 countries.

00:00:19.218 --> 00:00:22.121
The campus employs
1,700 professors

00:00:22.154 --> 00:00:24.457
teaching 300 programs
of study,

00:00:24.490 --> 00:00:27.326
and it's proud to be home
to 12 Nobel Prize winners.

00:00:27.359 --> 00:00:28.795
It is considered
one of the finest

00:00:28.828 --> 00:00:31.664
research universities
in the world.

00:00:31.697 --> 00:00:34.634
Recently, researchers at McGill
have embarked on a study

00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:38.571
that uses a brain scanning
device to read people's minds

00:00:38.604 --> 00:00:41.774
and implant thoughts
into their heads.

00:00:41.807 --> 00:00:44.110
Or so their subjects think.

00:00:44.143 --> 00:00:46.813
Now, the same device may be able
to help kids with ADHD,

00:00:46.846 --> 00:00:49.582
anxiety,
obsessive-compulsive disorder,

00:00:49.615 --> 00:00:54.487
migraines,
Tourette's and more.

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:57.690 align:start size:53% position:47%
This study is not
about technology.

00:00:57.723 --> 00:01:00.760 align:start size:78% position:22%
The MRI machine behind me
may look impressive,

00:01:00.793 --> 00:01:02.228 align:start size:63% position:38%
but it's a sham.

00:01:02.261 --> 00:01:04.597 align:start size:63% position:38%
It's deactivated,
nonfunctioning.

00:01:04.630 --> 00:01:06.599 align:start size:63% position:38%
What this study
is really about

00:01:06.632 --> 00:01:09.602 align:start size:63% position:38%
is faith in science.

00:01:09.635 --> 00:01:12.772 align:start size:63% position:38%
It's about the power
of thoughts to heal.

00:01:19.378 --> 00:01:23.083
All you need is the power
of suggestion.

00:01:24.884 --> 00:01:28.088
[theme music playing]

00:01:37.763 --> 00:01:40.833
A placebo is something
that shouldn't work,

00:01:40.866 --> 00:01:43.136
but due to the power
of suggestion

00:01:43.169 --> 00:01:46.539
and because of the strength
of our belief, does.

00:01:46.572 --> 00:01:49.675
But we don't fully understand
yet how they work.

00:01:49.708 --> 00:01:52.445 line:0%
<i> There could be
 an evolutionary explanation.</i>

00:01:52.478 --> 00:01:55.181 line:0%
<i> For example, if a small child
 hurts themselves,</i>

00:01:55.214 --> 00:01:58.718
<i> negative symptoms like pain
 and crying can be good.</i>

00:01:58.751 --> 00:02:01.487
<i> They keep the child safe
 and still</i>

00:02:01.520 --> 00:02:03.656
<i> while signaling adults
 to come help.</i>

00:02:03.689 --> 00:02:05.191
<i> When help arrives,</i>

00:02:05.224 --> 00:02:07.426
<i> even if it
 has no active effect,</i>

00:02:07.459 --> 00:02:08.794
<i> the child's brain may feel</i>

00:02:08.827 --> 00:02:11.230
<i> it has permission to redirect</i>

00:02:11.263 --> 00:02:13.266
<i> resources away
 from seeking help</i>

00:02:13.299 --> 00:02:15.635
<i> and onto actually healing.</i>

00:02:15.668 --> 00:02:18.538
<i> Modern medicine has found
 a way to harness this power</i>

00:02:18.571 --> 00:02:20.873
<i> by prescribing placebos.</i>

00:02:20.906 --> 00:02:23.476
But not all placebos work
the same.

00:02:23.509 --> 00:02:26.445 align:start position:0%
For example, a sugar pill
will help your headache more

00:02:26.478 --> 00:02:28.214 size:84% position:42%
if given to you by a doctor

00:02:28.247 --> 00:02:29.849 align:start position:0%
than by a poker buddy.

00:02:29.882 --> 00:02:32.952
And the color
of the placebo matters, too.

00:02:32.985 --> 00:02:36.255 align:start position:0%
A blue pill will work
to make you feel calm

00:02:36.288 --> 00:02:37.857 size:75% position:38%
better than a white pill

00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:40.660 align:start position:0%
because blue
is a more calming color.

00:02:40.693 --> 00:02:43.262 align:start position:0% line:0%
And a red pill
will keep you awake

00:02:43.295 --> 00:02:44.564 size:75% position:38% line:0%
and give you more energy

00:02:44.597 --> 00:02:46.432 align:start position:0% line:0%
than a blue pill will.

00:02:46.465 --> 00:02:48.868 align:start position:0% line:0%
A capsule will work
better than a pill

00:02:48.901 --> 00:02:52.205 align:start position:0% line:0%
because it looks
more important.

00:02:56.275 --> 00:03:00.246 align:start position:0%
Also, an injection will work
better than a capsule

00:03:00.279 --> 00:03:02.582 align:start position:0%
because it seems
more serious

00:03:02.615 --> 00:03:04.450 align:start position:0%
and potent.

00:03:04.483 --> 00:03:07.253
There's even evidence
that fake or sham surgeries

00:03:07.286 --> 00:03:08.754
have positive effects.

00:03:08.787 --> 00:03:10.489
It may be fake medicine,

00:03:10.522 --> 00:03:12.491
but the effects can be real.

00:03:12.524 --> 00:03:15.528
And not just because the patient
feels better psychologically.

00:03:15.561 --> 00:03:17.697
We're talking
real physical healing,

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:20.633
thanks to the power
of the brain.

00:03:27.940 --> 00:03:29.742
<i> I traveled to Montreal</i>

00:03:29.775 --> 00:03:31.310
<i> to meet local children
 struggling</i>

00:03:31.343 --> 00:03:32.845
<i> with debilitating behavioral</i>

00:03:32.878 --> 00:03:34.780
<i> and neurological conditions</i>

00:03:34.813 --> 00:03:36.949
<i> who would soon find out
 whether their afflictions</i>

00:03:36.982 --> 00:03:39.986
<i> could be cured
 by the power of suggestion.</i>

00:03:40.019 --> 00:03:41.687
-This is Malaya.
-Hi.

00:03:41.720 --> 00:03:43.689 align:start size:63% position:38%
Malaya. I'm Michael.
Nice to meet you.

00:03:43.722 --> 00:03:45.958
<i> Twelve-year-old Malaya
 suffers from a common</i>

00:03:45.991 --> 00:03:48.027
<i> skin ailment, eczema.</i>

00:03:48.060 --> 00:03:49.562 line:92%
<i> But she has also developed</i>

00:03:49.595 --> 00:03:53.499
<i> a skin picking disorder,
 dermatillomania.</i>

00:03:53.532 --> 00:03:56.736 align:start position:0%
You're starting high school
what, like this year?

00:03:56.769 --> 00:03:57.903 align:start size:50% position:50% line:0%
Early September.

00:03:57.936 --> 00:04:00.039 align:start position:0% line:0%
Wow, that's a big step.

00:04:00.072 --> 00:04:02.341 align:start position:0%
So, what kind of things,
like, worry you,

00:04:02.374 --> 00:04:04.477 align:start position:0%
uh, given the symptoms
that you have?

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:06.479 align:start size:66% position:34%
Probably the picking.

00:04:06.512 --> 00:04:07.847
-Of your skin?
-[Malaya] Yeah.

00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:09.649 size:81% position:59%
I don't know, I find
it satisfying to pick.

00:04:09.682 --> 00:04:10.783 align:start size:63% position:38%
It's kind of gross.

00:04:10.816 --> 00:04:12.285 align:start position:0%
Why do you think
you can't stop?

00:04:12.318 --> 00:04:13.619 align:start size:50% position:50%
I'm not sure.

00:04:13.652 --> 00:04:15.855 align:start position:0%
Have you tried
different things

00:04:15.888 --> 00:04:17.423 align:start position:0%
that'll help you stop?

00:04:17.456 --> 00:04:18.758 align:start size:75% position:25%
Yeah. Like, in my mind,

00:04:18.791 --> 00:04:21.294 align:start size:75% position:25%
I'm just like,
"Today you won't pick.

00:04:21.327 --> 00:04:23.296 align:start size:75% position:25%
You are gonna get rid
of this eczema."

00:04:23.329 --> 00:04:25.031
And then after,
I'm just like,

00:04:25.064 --> 00:04:27.433 align:start size:75% position:25%
"Oh, wait. My face is,
like, bleeding."

00:04:27.466 --> 00:04:29.635
-Yeah. Is it embarrassing?
-Yeah.

00:04:29.668 --> 00:04:32.471
I like to wear long sleeves
because my arms are, like,

00:04:32.504 --> 00:04:34.940 align:start size:75% position:25%
if they're really bad,
I'm gonna try to wear
long sleeves.

00:04:34.973 --> 00:04:37.476 align:start position:0%
How are your arms now?

00:04:37.509 --> 00:04:40.980 align:start size:75% position:25%
It's, like, really bad.
So, as you can see--

00:04:41.013 --> 00:04:42.315 align:start position:0%
And it's all just
from scratching and picking?

00:04:42.348 --> 00:04:43.349 align:start size:47% position:53%
Yeah.

00:04:44.817 --> 00:04:46.719
<i> Twelve-year-old Nicholas
 was troubled</i>

00:04:46.752 --> 00:04:49.455
<i> by debilitating
 migraine headaches.</i>

00:04:49.488 --> 00:04:51.457 align:start size:66% position:34%
So, what do you wanna
be when you grow up?

00:04:51.490 --> 00:04:53.726 align:start position:0% line:0%
Like, I really,
really wanna be,

00:04:53.759 --> 00:04:56.329 align:start position:0% line:0%
uh, probably like an NHL
or an MLB player,

00:04:56.362 --> 00:04:57.730 align:start position:0%
one of those two.

00:04:57.763 --> 00:05:00.599
<i> Nicholas's love of sports
 is unfortunately also</i>

00:05:00.632 --> 00:05:02.802
<i> the original source
 of his suffering.</i>

00:05:02.835 --> 00:05:04.403 align:start size:19% position:81%
Nice.

00:05:04.436 --> 00:05:07.406 size:84% position:58%
My first head injury,
which was concussion,

00:05:07.439 --> 00:05:08.941 align:start size:75% position:25%
I hit my head
on a soccer post.

00:05:08.974 --> 00:05:12.011
And then I hit my head
in a game of, uh, hockey.

00:05:12.044 --> 00:05:15.581
Uh, after that, I had headaches
every single day.

00:05:15.614 --> 00:05:17.516 align:start size:63% position:38%
I was throwing up,
having auras--

00:05:17.549 --> 00:05:19.018 align:start size:75% position:25%
they're like, uh, colors

00:05:19.051 --> 00:05:20.886 align:start size:63% position:38%
that you see before
you have a headache.

00:05:20.919 --> 00:05:22.521 align:start size:63% position:38%
I wasn't able to go
to school,

00:05:22.554 --> 00:05:24.490 align:start size:63% position:38%
and then we went
to the hospital

00:05:24.523 --> 00:05:26.525 align:start size:63% position:38%
and into their
concussion program.

00:05:26.558 --> 00:05:28.627 align:start size:63% position:38%
 Can I see
 his migraine chart?

00:05:28.660 --> 00:05:31.997 align:start position:0% line:0%
Oh, sure. Yeah. We have
almost two years' worth.

00:05:32.030 --> 00:05:33.866 align:start position:0%
Severe headaches here,
severe migraines.

00:05:33.899 --> 00:05:36.469
-[Michael] Every day?
-[Danielle] Every single day.

00:05:36.502 --> 00:05:38.104 align:start position:0%
This has turned
his world upside down.

00:05:39.905 --> 00:05:42.875
<i> Nathan was diagnosed with ADHD</i>

00:05:42.908 --> 00:05:45.111
<i> and impulse control disorder.</i>

00:05:45.144 --> 00:05:47.546 align:start position:0%
I'd love to hear especially
about you, Nathan.

00:05:47.579 --> 00:05:48.914 align:start position:0%
First of all,
how old are you?

00:05:48.947 --> 00:05:50.616 line:0%
-Nine.
-[Michael] Nine.

00:05:50.649 --> 00:05:52.818 line:0%
-How old you are?
-[Michael] How old
do you think I am?

00:05:52.851 --> 00:05:55.421 line:0%
-Thirty.
-That's a very good guess.

00:05:55.454 --> 00:05:57.590
-I'm 31.
-Ooh.

00:05:57.623 --> 00:06:00.626 size:81% position:41%
So, tell me about, like,
before Nathan's diagnosis.

00:06:00.659 --> 00:06:03.462 align:start position:0% line:0%
What were kind of the symptoms
you were seeing?

00:06:03.495 --> 00:06:06.932 align:start size:81% position:19% line:0%
Tantrums all the time, um,

00:06:06.965 --> 00:06:08.868 align:start size:63% position:38%
just an inability
to reach him,

00:06:08.901 --> 00:06:11.036 align:start size:75% position:25%
to communicate to him,
to connect to him,

00:06:11.069 --> 00:06:12.605 align:start size:81% position:19%
that was the main symptom.

00:06:12.638 --> 00:06:14.774 align:start position:0%
And what did you
think of this, Nathan?

00:06:14.807 --> 00:06:17.510 align:start position:0%
Were you like, "Why are
my parents not happy?"

00:06:19.545 --> 00:06:21.514
-Why weren't you?
-[Nathan] I don't know.

00:06:21.547 --> 00:06:23.583
Maybe because I have problems.

00:06:24.750 --> 00:06:27.987 align:start position:0%
And as far as,
like, behavior.

00:06:28.020 --> 00:06:29.789 align:start size:50% position:50%
Impulsivity,
hyperactivity,

00:06:29.822 --> 00:06:31.690 align:start size:63% position:38%
and you're always,
always on the edge,

00:06:31.723 --> 00:06:33.159 align:start size:72% position:28%
always stressed--
what is he gonna touch,

00:06:33.192 --> 00:06:35.127 align:start size:66% position:34%
where is he gonna go,
what is he gonna do.

00:06:35.160 --> 00:06:37.930
<i> These families had tried
 conventional methods</i>

00:06:37.963 --> 00:06:40.766
<i> to treat their children
 with little success.</i>

00:06:40.799 --> 00:06:42.802
<i> But they were about
 to find out</i>

00:06:42.835 --> 00:06:44.870
<i> whether their symptoms
 could be alleviated</i>

00:06:44.903 --> 00:06:47.773
<i> using an accessory-assisted
 placebo,</i>

00:06:47.806 --> 00:06:50.576
<i> a fake non-functioning
 MRI machine.</i>

00:06:50.609 --> 00:06:53.145
<i> This groundbreaking study
 of the power of suggestion</i>

00:06:53.178 --> 00:06:57.049
<i> and action is the brainchild
 of pioneering researchers</i>

00:06:57.082 --> 00:07:00.519
<i> at McGill University's
 esteemed Raz Lab.</i>

00:07:00.552 --> 00:07:02.621 line:0%
We study a whole bunch
of different mind-body

00:07:02.654 --> 00:07:04.123 line:0%
interaction topics--
suggestion,

00:07:04.156 --> 00:07:06.058
hypnosis, placebo effects.

00:07:06.091 --> 00:07:09.495
Anytime the mind is regulating
the body or vice versa,

00:07:09.528 --> 00:07:11.030
that's a topic
that we study.

00:07:11.063 --> 00:07:12.998 align:start size:63% position:38%
Now, you said
the word "placebo."

00:07:13.031 --> 00:07:15.935 align:start size:63% position:38%
And the device
that we are using

00:07:15.968 --> 00:07:17.970 align:start size:63% position:38%
is a sham scanner.

00:07:18.003 --> 00:07:19.738 align:start size:63% position:38%
<i> Tell me about
 the scanner.</i>

00:07:19.771 --> 00:07:22.241
[Jay]<i> What we do
 with the MRI scanners is</i>

00:07:22.274 --> 00:07:26.245 align:start size:81% position:19%
we stack so many different
layers of deception.

00:07:26.278 --> 00:07:28.681
In their head, this is
a proper neuroscience study

00:07:28.714 --> 00:07:30.783
done at the neurological
institute.

00:07:30.816 --> 00:07:31.984
And that's why we wear
lab coats.

00:07:32.017 --> 00:07:33.118 size:88% position:44%
That's why we have
all of this

00:07:33.151 --> 00:07:34.720 size:81% position:41%
scientific-looking
equipment.

00:07:34.753 --> 00:07:37.022 align:start position:0%
By the time they've actually
started the study,

00:07:37.055 --> 00:07:38.691
they've already in their mind

00:07:38.724 --> 00:07:41.227 align:start position:0%
built up all these different
layers of credibility.

00:07:41.260 --> 00:07:44.196 size:78% position:39%
They really believe that
what we're doing is real.

00:07:44.229 --> 00:07:46.599
[Dr. Veissiere] What's
interesting is that children,

00:07:46.632 --> 00:07:48.834 line:0%
they're not immune to the power
of neuroenchantment.

00:07:48.867 --> 00:07:51.103
-Neuroenchantment?
-Neuroenchantment.

00:07:51.136 --> 00:07:53.239
-What does that mean?
-So, it's this idea

00:07:53.272 --> 00:07:55.708 align:start position:0%
that there is some kind
of medical magic.

00:07:55.741 --> 00:07:58.177 align:start position:0%
There is immense power
that is attached

00:07:58.210 --> 00:07:59.979 align:start position:0%
to the culture
of neuroscience

00:08:00.012 --> 00:08:03.516
<i> whereby neuroscientific props
 and accessories</i>

00:08:03.549 --> 00:08:05.718
<i> have more healing power,</i>

00:08:05.751 --> 00:08:07.553
<i> more physiological effects,</i>

00:08:07.586 --> 00:08:10.256
because culturally
people believe that they do.

00:08:10.289 --> 00:08:13.025 align:start position:0%
I mean, the same kind
of cultural cognitive mechanisms

00:08:13.058 --> 00:08:15.661 align:start position:0%
are at play
in religious systems.

00:08:15.694 --> 00:08:18.097
So, here we are praying
to the gods of neuroscience

00:08:18.130 --> 00:08:19.798
and biomedicine.

00:08:19.831 --> 00:08:22.201 align:start size:63% position:38%
Talk to me about
the ethics of lying.

00:08:22.234 --> 00:08:23.903 align:start position:0%
The work we do
with children

00:08:23.936 --> 00:08:25.804 align:start position:0%
actually does not
involve lying.

00:08:25.837 --> 00:08:28.107
We tell them at first
that everything that they see

00:08:28.140 --> 00:08:30.676 size:84% position:42%
and everything that we do
in the lab is a suggestion.

00:08:30.709 --> 00:08:33.178
We explain to them
that suggestion is a way to tap

00:08:33.211 --> 00:08:35.114 align:start position:0%
into the power
of their mind.

00:08:35.147 --> 00:08:37.783 size:78% position:39%
We keep emphasizing even
as they go in the scanner

00:08:37.816 --> 00:08:41.287 align:start position:0%
that it is their mind
and their brain
that is doing the healing,

00:08:41.320 --> 00:08:45.124 align:start position:0%
that they're basically
reprogramming their own brain.

00:08:45.157 --> 00:08:48.193
<i> The parents knew
that the scanner was a placebo.</i>

00:08:48.226 --> 00:08:50.095
<i> But for the study to work,
 the children</i>

00:08:50.128 --> 00:08:52.598
<i> had to believe
 in the procedure.</i>

00:08:52.631 --> 00:08:54.266
<i> So, before they visited
 the lab,</i>

00:08:54.299 --> 00:08:56.168
<i> I enlisted
 a few YouTuber friends</i>

00:08:56.201 --> 00:08:59.338
<i> to help raise
 their expectations.</i>

00:08:59.371 --> 00:09:00.639 align:start position:0%
[Veronica]<i> Hey, guys.</i>

00:09:00.672 --> 00:09:02.975 align:start position:0% line:0%
<i>Today, we have
a huge surprise for you</i>

00:09:03.008 --> 00:09:04.843 align:start position:0% line:0%
<i>about something
brand new in science</i>

00:09:04.876 --> 00:09:06.011 align:start position:0%
<i>that could affect you!</i>

00:09:06.044 --> 00:09:07.279 size:75% position:38%
Oh, I know them.

00:09:07.312 --> 00:09:08.781 align:start size:75% position:25%
<i> Well, today,
 we learned about</i>

00:09:08.814 --> 00:09:10.082 align:start size:75% position:25%
<i> this amazing new machie</i>

00:09:10.115 --> 00:09:11.584 align:start size:78% position:22%
<i> that teaches kids' brais</i>

00:09:11.617 --> 00:09:13.252 align:start size:72% position:28%
<i> how to heal super-fas.</i>

00:09:13.285 --> 00:09:15.254 align:start size:88% position:13% line:0%
<i> We really hope that you get
 the chance in person</i>

00:09:15.287 --> 00:09:16.956 align:start size:63% position:38% line:0%
<i> to see how
 this machine works.</i>

00:09:16.989 --> 00:09:18.090 align:start position:0%
<i>With a little help
from the machine,</i>

00:09:18.123 --> 00:09:20.092 align:start position:0%
<i>you can focus better,
be more confident.</i>

00:09:20.125 --> 00:09:22.227 align:start position:0%
<i>-And it can even take away
some headaches.
-Awesome.</i>

00:09:22.260 --> 00:09:23.796 align:start size:75% position:25%
[Vanessa]<i> Not too many
 people get the chance</i>

00:09:23.829 --> 00:09:25.798 align:start size:75% position:25%
<i> to have this
 awesome experience,</i>

00:09:25.831 --> 00:09:28.167 align:start size:88% position:13%
<i> but we hear
 the scientists in Canada--</i>

00:09:28.200 --> 00:09:30.035
-I'm going to have it?
-Yeah.

00:09:30.068 --> 00:09:32.004 align:start size:63% position:38%
